# The build context is deliberately narrow: everything is excluded and only the
# four trees the image needs are let back in, then the heavy directories inside
# them are excluded again -- by NAME, with the files bin/BUNDLE.txt actually
# lists re-included one by one.
#
# This is not micro-optimisation, and the exceptions are not decoration.
# `k6/tools/` is 208 MB in this checkout and 187 MB of it is `dione-evidence`,
# of which the bundle lists exactly two files -- because a setup-time selftest
# opens them, fail-closed. An over-eager exclusion here does not fail the
# build; it produces an image that dies in the `setup` stage on a rented box,
# which is the same shape as the bug that had a MiniMax root capture die on
# GGUF test data that was never bundled. `bin/selftest_container.py` rung C5
# therefore checks every BUNDLE.txt entry against these patterns.
*
!bin
!registry
!k6
k6/*
!k6/tools
!k6/patches-v2
k6/tools/dione-evidence/*
!k6/tools/dione-evidence/bf16-config.json
!k6/tools/dione-evidence/bf16-index.json
k6/tools/newarch-stagea-evidence
k6/tools/glm53-stagea-evidence
k6/tools/layer-outer-evidence
k6/tools/hidden-replay-evidence
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
